\DOC ADD_IBT_TAC_PARAMETRIZED

\TYPE {ADD_IBT_TAC_PARAMETRIZED : thm -> thm -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Proves an {ensures} correctness goal for a program whose byte list carries an
extra prefix, by combining a bridging equation between the full and offset
program with an already-established correctness theorem, closing the goal
outright.

\DESCRIBE
{bridge_th} is an equation stating that the full machine-code list for the
program equals the four-byte prefix appended to the code list for the shifted
program; {th} is the previously proved correctness theorem for the shifted
program, supplying the actual specification content. The goal's conclusion is a
universally quantified (and sometimes existentially prefixed) implication from
{riprel32_within_bounds} and nonoverlapping side conditions to an {ensures}
statement about the full code list.
{
   A ?- t
   ========================  ADD_IBT_TAC_PARAMETRIZED bridge_th th
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces this single outcome occurs, on goals with no assumptions
and of this specific {ensures}-specification shape.

\ENDDOC
